# RULE: Architecture Boundaries

This is a mandatory Cursor rule.

It defines what agents must never violate while working on the Enterprise Softphone Platform.

## Required Layering

The architecture has six layers:

```txt
UI
↓
Application
↓
Domain
↓
Ports
↓
Adapters
↓
Infrastructure
```

Dependencies must point inward.

## Forbidden Dependencies

Never introduce:

- UI -> SIP library
- UI -> Electron API
- UI -> repository
- UI -> filesystem
- UI -> WebSocket protocol
- UI -> adapter implementation
- Domain -> React
- Domain -> Electron
- Domain -> JsSIP
- Domain -> Zustand
- Domain -> browser APIs
- Domain -> Node APIs
- Domain -> storage
- Domain -> infrastructure
- Store -> SIP library
- Store -> Electron API
- Store -> repository
- Adapter -> UI

## Required Entry Points

Business operations must enter through Use Cases:

- `MakeCallUseCase`
- `AnswerCallUseCase`
- `HangupCallUseCase`
- `HoldCallUseCase`
- `TransferCallUseCase`
- `RegisterAccountUseCase`
- `ChangeAgentStatusUseCase`

UI may call Use Cases or UI-facing application facades only.

## Telephony Boundary

All telephony operations must pass through Call Engine.

Never:

- call JsSIP from React
- call JsSIP from Zustand
- mutate SIP sessions in UI
- store raw SIP sessions in Domain
- expose JsSIP objects through ports

Allowed:

- `TelephonyGateway` port
- `JsSipTelephonyAdapter` implementation
- typed Domain Events from adapter events

## OCP Boundary

OCP is optional.

Core telephony must work without OCP.

Never make Domain or Call Engine depend on:

- OCP WebSocket
- OCP statuses
- OCP campaign events
- host-page globals

Use an `OperatorPlatformGateway` or integration plugin.

## Headset Boundary

Headset vendors are adapters.

Never couple Domain or Call Engine to:

- Jabra
- Poly
- EPOS
- WebHID-specific payloads

Hardware events must map to application commands.

## Store Boundary

Stores are projections.

Stores may:

- receive events
- update read models
- expose selectors

Stores must not:

- execute business rules
- call SIP
- call Electron
- call repositories
- call WebSocket
- own orchestration

## State Machine Boundary

Call state must be explicit.

Use canonical states:

- `Idle`
- `Ringing`
- `Connecting`
- `Active`
- `Held`
- `Transferring`
- `Conference`
- `Ending`
- `Ended`
- `Failed`

Never use boolean flags as primary state:

- `isHeld`
- `isEnded`
- `isConnecting`
- `isTransferred`

## Completion Check

Before finishing any change, verify:

- Domain remains framework-independent.
- UI does not access adapters.
- Stores remain projections.
- Telephony actions pass through Call Engine.
- OCP remains optional.
- External library objects do not cross ports.
